1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,486
The gun shown here is the latest R zero six geometry

2
00:00:03,486 --> 00:00:11,197
Its one hundred and forty one component instances are available as a native SolidWorks assembly and as neutral STEP

3
00:00:11,197 --> 00:00:17,500
The target is a two inch diameter aluminium disc, three point one seven five millimetres thick

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:25,144
R zero five revised the clamp contact shoulder and aperture, and changed the twelve clamp screws to M three by ten

5
00:00:25,144 --> 00:00:28,832
The target back remains seated on the same cooler datum

6
00:00:28,832 --> 00:00:39,895
The complete gun was raised one point one seven five millimetres in the chamber so the target front and the default one hundred millimetre substrate gap remain fixed

7
00:00:39,895 --> 00:00:45,125
A nominal one millimetre gap separates the live clamp from the grounded shield

8
00:00:45,125 --> 00:00:51,629
Screw preload, thermal contact, tolerances, and electrical qualification remain engineering work.
